{
  "note": "Chronology: the sweep ran 16:50:44Z-16:53:50Z with harness 8e33f080. The executor then inspected the first generated report (decision-bearing results) and audited it; HC1-HC3 were committed at 17:05:52Z and 17:06:34Z (6f3a6e83, e33d4339). Codex review round 1 found HC4-HC5; they were committed at 17:26:51Z (dcd6f34a). Every correction follows inspection of results and implements registered text; no registered rule changed. No verifier channel was re-executed: HC1-HC3 re-apply the mapping to retained observations, and HC4/HC5 re-run R1-O2 from the retained forced emission with the pinned Calor.Runtime.dll. Run-time values are retained in every attempt (runtimeClassification, runtimeO2) and in <baseline>/case-results.runtime-8e33f080.jsonl.",
  "runtimeHarnessCommit": "8e33f08019303cf805e5098775032face6017a27",
  "reclassifyHarnessCommit": "15aa06ca4c017e86a91954fc812220f7f521b6bc (behavior-identical compaction of dcd6f34a; outputs byte-identical)",
  "corrections": [
    {
      "id": "HC1",
      "registeredText": "channels.CH-IMPLICATION: \"Each IMPL template carries contracts in exactly one direction ... its outcome is read from the Calor0815 info diagnostic text ('Precondition weakening proven' or the postcondition counterpart: Proven) ... Any other Calor0815 on the case is archived, not adjudicated.\"",
      "defect": "The run-time harness read any Calor0815 as Proven. B1 and N1 also emit the other direction's Calor0815 when that direction has no contracts, so a Failed (LSP-violation error) template direction was mapped to Proven.",
      "fix": "Only the template's own direction (the Calor0815 / Calor0816 / LSP-violation text naming that direction) is adjudicated."
    },
    {
      "id": "HC2",
      "registeredText": "observation.perCase guard observation: \"in the forced emission it must be present.\"",
      "defect": "The run-time harness searched the forced emission for one exception type per obligation kind. B1 emits RefinementReturn guards as InvalidOperationException(\"Return value violates refinement type ...\") and inline parameter refinements as \"Violation of inline refinement ...\", so present guards were reported absent (guard-elided-without-proof).",
      "fix": "Guard markers are the emitted guard texts per obligation kind: \"Proof obligation [\", \"Indexed-type bound violated\", \"Violation of refinement type\" or \"Violation of inline refinement\" (RefinementEntry), \"Return value violates refinement type\", \"Value violates refinement type\" (Subtype)."
    },
    {
      "id": "HC3",
      "registeredText": "caseResults.classes.spurious-refutation: \"Failed whose replayed counterexample model does not violate the property under O1\"",
      "defect": "The run-time harness treated models with string-typed parameters as not replayable, which made such Failed results no-claim without replay.",
      "fix": "String parameters are replayed from the SMT-LIB string literal Z3 prints. Arrays and user-type objects remain not replayable (the model has no length or field values)."
    },
    {
      "id": "HC4",
      "registeredText": "oracle.corroboration (R1-O2): the forced emission is executed on every O1 witness and the first 16 reached inputs",
      "defect": "The O1 point verdict ran the oracle body on the same input objects later passed to O2, so a body that mutates an (aliased) array changed the entry values O2 received (e.g. POST-ARRAY-ALIAS).",
      "fix": "O1 point verdicts and O2 receive independently recovered input tuples. O2 was re-run for every executed attempt from the retained forced emission (no compiler call); no class changed and no semantic-divergence appeared."
    },
    {
      "id": "HC5",
      "registeredText": "oracle.corroboration (R1-O2): the emitted function is called with the tuple (or the template replay expression)",
      "defect": "The replay driver declared oracle-defined (Box) and object parameters with the oracle CLR type, so 7 cases per baseline (OBL-UNGATED-REFERENCE 001-005, GEN-REFUSAL 002, 004) did not compile and O2 did not run.",
      "fix": "Such parameters are copied by member name into the emitted type and bound dynamically; an input the emitted signature cannot accept (new object() for a double[] parameter) is recorded as not-run-input-not-representable. After HC5, O2 runs on 675 of 684 applicable cases per baseline; the other 9 are cases the compiler itself rejected (Calor1002), so there is no runnable emission."
    }
  ],
